# Issue #12 item N2 (INV-4): every go2rtc-proxied location is gone once N2's
# nginx patch lands, and one of the five (/live/mse/api/ws) is replaced by a
# new location proxying to G2's fMP4-over-WebSocket packager
# (corvette-media-bridge, crates/corvette-media-bridge/src/ws_repackager.rs)
# instead of having no successor at all. Established directly against a real
# nginx serving the patched config, with no go2rtc upstream running at all
# (`.agents/issue-12/evidence/N2-mutation.log`), not assumed: nginx's own
# location-matching means the five removed routes do NOT all fail the same
# way.
#
# The three /live/* paths below (no other /live/* location claims them) fall
# through all the way to the site's own SPA shell, at 200 -- the same
# "unmatched path" failure mode /go2rtc/stream.html above documents, and
# tabled here the same way.
#
# The other two, /api/go2rtc/api and /api/go2rtc/webrtc, are deliberately
# NOT tabled: once their own location is gone they fall under the broader,
# pre-existing `location /api/` prefix and proxy through to Frigate's own API
# instead of the SPA shell -- confirmed in the harness only against a stub
# standing in for Frigate, which is not a source for what Frigate's real API
# answers for a path it never defined. Re-verify these two against the live
# pod once N2/F1/K1 ship and table them then, rather than guessing Frigate's
# real 404 shape now.
#
# NOT YET the live deployment's own behaviour, same caveat as N1's block
# above: these describe the TARGET contract, become a real pod-mode
# assertion once N2, F1 and K1 ship together, and use the same "front_door"
# placeholder camera name N1's own rows use.
/live/mse/api/ws | 200 | text/html | contains:id="root";contains:/assets/main-
/live/webrtc/api/ws | 200 | text/html | contains:id="root";contains:/assets/main-
/live/webrtc/webrtc.html | 200 | text/html | contains:id="root";contains:/assets/main-

# The new replacement location, /live/mse/ws/<camera>, is deliberately NOT
# tabled either, for a different reason than the two /api/go2rtc/* omissions
# above: unlike G3's HLS packager (a plain HTTP server, which is why
# /live/hls/front_door above is a real, tabled row), G2 is a WebSocket
# listener (`ws_repackager::handle_connection`, a real
# `tokio_tungstenite::accept_hdr_async` handshake) -- route_parity.sh's own
# plain GET, with no Upgrade header, is not a real client request this
# route ever actually serves, so a status/body pinned from that GET would
# not describe G2's real contract. The harness proved something narrower and
# real instead (`.agents/issue-12/evidence/N2-mutation.log`): nginx's own
# proxy_pass wiring reaches the corvette_fmp4_ws upstream and forwards
# whatever a stand-in backend answers, which is what this item's Verify step
# asks for. Table a real row here once a WebSocket-capable check exists to
# state its expectation honestly.
